==
== <CharacterWeights> - per-point Power granted by each character stat:
==   LevelWeight        * character Level
==   StrengthWeight      * total Strength
==   DexterityWeight     * total Dexterity
==   VitalityWeight      * total Vitality
==   EnergyWeight        * total Energy
==   LeadershipWeight    * total Leadership
==   MasterLevelWeight   * Master Level (Master class only)
==   MasterPointWeight   * Master Skill points spent (Master class only)
==   CultivationWeight, TitleWeight, ReincarnationWeight - reserved for
==     future systems, currently unused by CalcLucChien().
==
== <ItemWeights><Item .../></ItemWeights> - Power granted per equipped item
==   (checked against the 12 equipment slots):
==   IndexMin/IndexMax  Item index range this row applies to.
==   BaseWeight         Flat Power for having any item in range equipped.
==   RefineWeight       * item +Level (refine level).
==   RankWeight         * gItemManager.GetItemLevel(index) (item's base
==                         rank/tier, independent of refine level).
==   SkillOptionWeight  Flat Power if the item has the Skill option.
==   LuckOptionWeight   Flat Power if the item has the Luck option.
==   LifeOptionWeight   * the item's Option (Life/Defense) magnitude.
==   ExcellentOptionWeight  * number of Excellent lines on the item.
==   HarmonyOptionWeight    Flat Power if the item has a Harmony option.
==   Option380Weight        Flat Power if the item has the 380 option.
==   AncientOptionWeight    Flat Power if the item is an Ancient (Set) item.
==   SocketOptionWeight     * number of socketed lines on the item.
==
== You can add extra <Item> rows (even for a single specific item, e.g.
== IndexMin="19" IndexMax="19") to give bonus Power for VIP items or wings -
== all matching rows are added together, they don't replace each other.
== Modify only if you know what you're doing!
============================================================
-->
